  "worked_solution": "- Statement I is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/4efadc7686e7d8845c98d97e16c44a19d233ae5ef50df160ce12b1823725966d.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/da1fb5e45ddfc41a8a9ff592ade9e5f2d5411e07b8e6ed1cf4ddad7e5841f6ae.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14134102/assets/4fd5a2ee4afd7c9d61b4d8e20cf676c602167d1d8f21a6392f36bcfeb54a8f25.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
